ched and then based on  the complexity of it how funny we think  it is  how dumb we think it is if we think a  friendship move is dumb that's usually a  really good sign  the whole point of these things is to be  silly to be the opposite of a fatality  to  get laughter out of somebody rather than  shock because we have  almost 40 friendship moves in the game a  lot of the ones that we did not use  i've somehow forgotten all about cedrion  if you're familiar with cetriana she's  all about balance and she's all about  good and evil so her friendship move is  also all about balance  she brings up a tree it's all about  nature and everything and then  generates a swing and is just swinging  and enjoying the balance of nature  it's not an elaborate friendship but it  certainly reflects  her personality dvora's friendship  she has always had ties with the insect  world  it actually starts out a little bit  dramatic she turns into a cocoon and  then the exact  opposite of what you're expecting  happens she basically bursts  out as a butterfly  [Applause]  the irony of she's always been the most  disgusting  representation of bugs and then kind of  coming out at the other end of the  spectrum with this butterfly  is quite fitting for her if we were to  give her a friendship move  aaron black aaron black is a  gunslinger we figured what is the most  non-threatening  use of guns that we can think of  i love the way this friendship move  starts  really dramatic you kind of see his head  tilting up almost like a clint eastwood  movie and then we quickly transition to  the carnival shooting gallery  you see glimpses of this idea used for  other friendships we're gonna see  something similar to that in the future  but  this whole how quickly he does a quick  shot  is probably one of my favorite kind of  like setting that's created  in in this friendship with aaron black  [Music]  frost like sub-zero having this kind of  cold power you knew it was going to have  something to do with ice  we decided to make an ice skating rink  one of my favorite things about this  particular  friendship is the animations we don't  have an ice skating rink in our motion  capture studio but somehow  our animation team and mocap team  duplicated the feeling  of ice skating and so she's skating  around the arena  her spinning move at the very end is is  particularly funny just because her head  stays still while her body kind of  rotates it i still don't know how those  guys pull that one off  much of what gives the realism in terms  of the feel and look with our games is  the fact that we  grab a lot of our animations through  motion capture so we have motion capture  talent come in we actually have them  perform the moves  for frost what was so particularly  exciting is the fact that we did not  have a skating rink so we could not  capture it live but  our animators can really perform  miracles as far as  getting the perfect look and feel so it  was a combination of  motion capture but a lot of animation  magic put on top of that  [Music]  fujin is the god of wind  naturally we wanted to have his  friendship move be of him flying a kite  he experiences all the struggles that a  kid does trying to get the kite in the  air  he decides to use his powers to make the  kite get off the ground what's so funny  about this friendship for  me is that he's actually skipping he's  skipping like a child which is  so kind of in the spirit of what  friendship moves are  in retrospect i wish that we had raiden  come out who's fujin's brother  flying the kite together i think it  would have been just that extra kind of  oomph for it  but we could not be happier with how  this friendship move turned out it's  easily one of the most playful in the  entire game  [Music]  garrus is one of the more almost random  and confusing  friendship moves we really were kind of  thinking what do you do with somebody  who has control over the sands of time  and of course you take those sands and  build a sand castle  one of the funny details i love about it  is the concentration that garrus has as  he's putting  that last flag on the top of the castle  he's got his tongue sticking out like he  just wants to put it in the exact right  place  my favorite part is his arms folding at  the end  looking at his masterpiece and he's so  happy and proud of it  that facial expression really sells the  whole thing for me  every single thing that we can do now is  something i wish we had  back in the day the technical struggles  way back  in the 90s were as big of a challenge as  coming up with the original ideas you  came up with the ideas and that was  great but then how do you do it when  you're kind of inside this box  now the box is gigantic it's a much  different challenge  but the capabilities are almost  limitless at this point  [Music]  jade's friendship is based on her staff  and when we were thinking what what do  kids do with something like a staff  the idea came up of a pinata so  jade swinging her staff at a pinata and  hundreds of pieces of candy flying out  is a very  fun friendship move for the team to make  what i love is the nuance of her  clapping  she's so happy with herself sitting down  with her legs crossed  and being almost kind of overwhelmed at  how much candy is in front of her  excitement almost taking over her as she  doesn't even know which piece of candy  to take so she's kind of frantically  grabbing every piece of candy that she  can even spot  that last moments there where she's just  in bliss  is really what sells this friendship  move most of the time we  look at the character in terms of their  abilities or something about their  costume that really stands  out based on those ideas what is  reasonable for us to create  we will pick the right one but normally  there is a  thread of a connection between the  character  and the friendship moves sometimes it's  a lot more of a  obvious connection and sometimes it's a  bit of a stretch but  those ones that are a bit of a stretch  are actually sometimes  the funnest ones jackie brings  jackie's friendship is the character  wanted to do something  something screwed up and that's the kind  of visual gag  jackie takes out like a punching bag and  she's using these kind of high-tech arms  you know kind of showing them off  punching this kind of rocking punching  bag she thinks that she gave it the  final blow and then it surprises  jackie and the audience and hits her  obviously because it's a friendship she  doesn't get  upset about it but it's certainly a bit  of a surprise and that's the kind of  visual gag so  hers is kind of like the first something  went wrong scenario that we have in the  game  jax jax's friendship move you can  almost called jax plays the sax  he is one of the simplest but stylized  friendship moves in the game  the music and the camera are some of the  biggest  parts of what gives this friendship move  the style he's got the subtle kind of  dancing going  the 70 shots with the multiple versions  of jax i love the background graphics  some people don't notice that when he  ends it he's actually playing the mortal  kombat theme  i love those kind of nuances that we put  in there johnny cage  johnny cage's friendship obviously has  to be related to showbiz  we wanted to add something unexpected so  he snaps his fingers  the lights go out and suddenly we're on  a stage  and he does this little dance number  with a  hat and cane the dancing is purposefully  hokey  that's part of the charm of it is he's  not a professional dancer but  he's so arrogant that he thinks he can  pull any of that stuff off  the little leg trick that he does at the  very end is funny and  when he ends it his hands are kind of  doing like a jazz hands thing  if you watch that friendship move a  number of times you'll pick up on little  nuances just like that  [Music]  john rambo's friendship is laser tag  i love the way it starts it has a clear  reference to the rambo movies where he's  suiting up  you think that something serious is  going on but when he clicks that gun  and you see it light up you know  something's different and boom we switch  to this  laser tag situation where he's in front  of and hiding behind the two  inflatable cover walls we go through a  sequence of his head  popping up taking shots at opponents  crawling between the two  shooting in a variety of ways it's a  classic  it's not what you think it is kind of  scenario  it'll be right between the eyes john  rambo helps finish out  our goal of getting as many 80s action  stars  in mortal kombat we've had terminator  we've had  robocop you are under arrest dirtbag and  now john rambo so  he really bookends that whole guest  character  roster that we have going machines are  either a benefit  or a hazard the thing about the licensed  characters that  was such a pleasant surprise for us was  that  we make the characters do such silly  things we were really concerned that the  the owners of the license would have an  issue with us doing something  as silly as he had but with rambo with  robocop with terminator  they were such great sports about it  that was one of the most pleasant  surprises in all of this was how  enthusiastic they were with having their  characters play along in this  silly portion of the game which is the  friendships  [Music]  joker has been in a number of nrs games  over the years  in mortal kombat 11 it's probably the  darkest representation that we've had  it was fun to see him back again in a  lighter  tone like jackie his friendship move is  another  something went wrong it starts off he's  trying to do something really sinister  with a gun  from out of the blue the batarang comes  out and hits him in the back of the head  he actually even references batman come  on  and then he switches over to  taking out some balloons at the end of  the day he says i'm sorry so  it's kind of like the batarang kind of  snapped him back into place into the  more  kinder gentler joker we really wanted to  have it be like a hint of batman come on  we certainly didn't want to have him  just come out and everybody's going to  be wanting to play him  if we actually created his model for the  game we've used joker three times before  mortal kombat versus dc  injustice 1 and injustice 2. in the t  rated games  we didn't want to kind of go crazy with  him in terms of  his his violent side and in mortal  kombat 11 that's when everything kind of  went loose  throwing joker into the mix with the  mortal kombat game  that's when you really get the  opportunity to take off all the reigns  and have him do crazy sick stuff  [Music]  cabal's friendship is probably one of  the most random friendships in the game  he zips onto the screen and there's this  gigantic xylophone that he starts  playing  probably what i'm most impressed with  this friendship  is the animation it is perfectly synced  to the music that is playing  you would never think that those were  two separate efforts that were done  by different team members again another  subtle reference to the mortal kombat  song i don't know how they managed to  time that so perfectly that's  a tribute to our animation and audio  team working together  as random as it was it's definitely one  of the more entertaining  friendship moves  kano was one of our more direct  friendship moves everybody thinks of  volcano  australian shrimp on the barbie so in  some respects we had to do  what we did kano uses his eye laser to  start a barbecue and he's got bratwurst  or something on there  if you look closely you will notice that  there are  shrimp on that barbecue i wish we had  him pick up a shrimp it would have been  a more direct reference but  for the people who are looking for those  details yes  i can confirm that there are shrimp on  that barbie  katana's friendship move is probably the  most friendliest  and perhaps innocent or childlike  since mortal kombat 11 