 would come down and  he would kind of do this dance  back in the day we had very little  memory to do it so he would just kind of  repeat the same  animation over and over again  this time it's a whole setup  you see the lights on the ground you see  the movements he has  choreography there's little hints of  like a saturday night fever point that  he does  the nuance again of this one i love is  he's a little bit  awkward he's not a professional dancer  there's a certain awkwardness which i  think is great it's a little  endearing dorkiness that he has where  he's doing the dance  but at the end of the day it's lou kang  he's got a lot of nobility  he hasn't really had much time to learn  about dancing and it kind of shows  molina's friendship we can call the  teddy bear tea party  if you notice the three teddy bears are  a teddy bear of molina  katana and jade and they're kind of like  our  famous female ninjas in a sense whenever  one of those characters is not in the  game everybody is clamoring for whatever  happened to this character we've gone  through that number of times  i love the way that when molina sets up  this tea party  she is constantly in the process of  making things even better she's  adjusting the teddy bears  she's pouring the tea her teddy bear  falls over she picks it up she's  applauding  she could not be happier to be there  that tea party  is just the perfect kind of summary of  the child-like  part of molina at the end of the day i  kind of wish we had done one of those  for the male ninjas it would have been  cool to see  scorpion sub-zero and rain or something  do the same thing  but we were able to do it with the  females and so that worked out great  [Music]  nightwell's friendship is pretty much an  animal act almost like a circus act  at first he pulls out this ring lights  on fire and you're just wondering is  this something more serious you see his  spirit  wolf come out what i love is the nuance  of him  tapping his leg enticing the the wolf to  jump through the hoop when it does  then everything cuts loose where the  eagles flying in  we see the bear in the background  balancing on the ball  and it's just this big staged circus act  what i found so entertaining about it is  nightwolf how intuitive he is you know  he's just coaxing the wolf to jump  through the hoop  and how proud he is holding the eagle at  the very end  like i taught these animals how to do  this it's such a funny situation to be  set up  this might actually be my favorite  friendship move  in the game easily it's in the top three  for me it starts  out with him splitting into three as a  clone and then  a jump rope sequence  this was a fun idea i think it worked  out great but  it was absolutely sold by the  performance  one of our motion capture talent his  name is nate he just went  crazy with it so you see all the nuances  i've never seen somebody in a motion  capture studio have  so much fun contributing to the spirit  of one of our cinematic moments the ink  splashes on the ground as his  hands and his feet make contact with it  is such a great detail of it but again  it's that performance and the animation  i've never seen something  communicate joy so much as to that guy  dancing and jumping rope at the same  time it was just such a such a great  performance  raiden's friendship along with liu kang  and baraka  and a number of other characters is a  nod to  their original friendship move raiden's  was called  kid thunder  and kid thunder makes a return in mortal  kombat 11.  a much more elaborate choreographed  light dance return so raiden summons can  thunder  and we hear that kind of familiar kid  thunder yell  we see this great light dance  performance the detail of him doing that  kind of  break dance moment and you'll notice if  you wait until the very end  he kind of gives this look to his dad  almost like he's looking for approval or  something like that you have to see  those  friendship moves a number of times to  pick all of those up  reigns friendship is the carnival water  gun  the way that it starts there's an irony  to it because he's sitting in a carnival  but the camera comes zooming in close  and he's holding his finger like a gun  like he's gonna do some kind of  action with it and then he points it at  this  party game that starts filling up the  balloon and it pops i love the way that  the  actual prize that he wins just falls  from the sky and he's holding it kind of  real proud of it and decides to show off  a little bit more  by creating a water spout coming from  his hand and that's kind of elevating  the  prize that he just won and it just kind  of stays there with him and the sense of  pride that he won this ridiculous  stuffed animal  [Music]  robocop's friendship is robocop does the  robot  it's a very retro dance sequence  which looks so ridiculous again it's  another example of how  grateful we are that the owners of these  licenses allowed us to do robocop doing  these 80s  90s 2000s dance nods the moonwalk and  all the things  is such a funny thing to see and  everybody will kind of make the  connection robocop doing the robot  again i'm so glad that they allowed us  to do something as silly as that  the music and the performance again this  is another one of those friendships  where  the performance just carries it the  motion capture that talent that we have  and the animators just  nailed the kind of spirit of what this  friendship move is trying to do  scorpion scorpion's friendship i guess  you can call the get over here giant  teddy bear  it was one of the first friendships that  we did where we kind of like set the  tone  of the remaining friendships in the game  he looks like he's going through one of  his  victory moves where he throws his spear  out the camera's this dramatic angle but  instead of some victim being pulled in  it's this big teddy bear and scorpion  just starts hugging him  one of the the details that are in that  particular friendship that i  hope people pick up on is as he's  hugging the teddy bear he looks up and  he  acknowledges the teddy bear one more  time and then continues to hug him and  it's really uh  so opposite of scorpion moment  that kind of defines what the spirit of  these friendship moves is intended to be  [Music]  shang tsung's friendship is like some of  the others  a tribute to his mortal kombat 2  friendship  he basically just kind of creates this  rainbow and it's kind of like this  universal symbol for love and everybody  getting along  which is great this time he has this  sinister look on his face and he's  creating this big spell  that you think something bad is gonna  come out of but then all of a sudden he  just reverts back to that pose with his  arms in the air  opening them up revealing the rainbow  and back to friendship  it's a little bit of a trick there where  he starts sinister  but then he kind of reverts back to that  friendship but it's one of our  quick and simple friendship moves in the  game  [Music]  shao khan along with aaron black and  rain  is a carnival-related friendship move  everybody knows shao khan  he's the big hammer what do you do with  a big hammer you test your might in a  sense and of course he's shao khan so he  breaks the bell at the top  everything shatters and he's all proud  of himself that's his kind of  i break the rules type of thing and  that's again the kind of trifecta of  carnival games that we have in mortal  kombat 11.  [Applause]  [Music]  shiva's friendship is she plays the wine  glasses  [Music]  this is easily the quietest smoothest  most mellow friendship that we have in  the game  with these characters that have four  arms we really try to think of something  novel for them to do  and shiva at the end of the day she  probably would prefer  peace and so we just put a whole bunch  of wine glasses in front of her and  she's just using all four  arms to play the soothing music very zen  but also one of the more simple  friendship moves in the game there's  nothing really complex about it just a  whole bunch of wine glasses that she  plays this little symphony on  [Music]  sindel's friendship is another quick and  simple one it's a bit of a gag  she takes out a wine glass and cindell  is known for  her voice her scream her ability to do  damage with this  voice and so you think that she's going  to scream and  shatter the wine glass but as she is  screaming the camera lens actually  cracks  she gives this sinister laugh  and she just takes a sip of the wine  because why not  i love the kind of little bit of a gag  that's in it where you think she's gonna  do the obvious and then  something else happens i think it might  be our only friendship move that kind of  breaks that fourth wall with the player  it's one of the kind of gag friendship  moves in our games there is no  like physical object that is the lens  throughout the game we use  different fields of view depending on  how dramatic we want to be with  something the mood that we're trying to  set but  that friendship is kind of playing on  that where it's kind of like hey don't  forget you're looking at this video game  through a lens  again that's that little nuance of kind  of breaking that fourth wall  [Music]  scarlett's friendship can be called the  masterpiece  starts out a little dark she's painting  with blood she goes from precision  where she's really concentrating and  then she goes to like these crazy  moments where she's throwing blood at  the canvas you're wondering what is this  gonna be  basically when she reveals it it's a  self-portrait it looks like a child  painted it makes no sense at all the  detail that i love about this one is the  facial expression that she has when it's  done  it's such a childish painting but as any  artist would be  she's just as proud as as can be with  this very basic self-portrait  [Music]  sonia blade's friendship is probably one  of the cuter friendships  in 